212
00:16:26,140 --> 00:16:28,000
They've brought judgment.

213
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:33,400
And God, it has to tell us that God, like, uses them to bring judgment on the Israelites.

214
00:16:34,860 --> 00:16:40,000
And so we've got God's people trapped in a godless nation.

215
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:49,500
And then Jeremiah writes them a letter of how they're supposed to live in this situation, in this situation that they find themselves in.

216
00:16:49,500 --> 00:16:51,520
I wonder what you might be thinking.

217
00:16:51,520 --> 00:16:59,880
What does a letter from 2,500 years ago to Jews in Babylon have anything to do with my life today?

218
00:16:59,880 --> 00:17:01,220
Right?

219
00:17:01,220 --> 00:17:01,680
Anybody?

220
00:17:01,680 --> 00:17:02,520
Anybody think of that?

221
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:07,880
Well, I've made this joke many times, but I'm going to do it again for that for the moment.

222
00:17:07,880 --> 00:17:10,840
I love when you ask the question of my not-long answer.

223
00:17:10,840 --> 00:17:12,280
Let me get there.

224
00:17:12,280 --> 00:17:17,440
And let me start with this quote from my friend, Josh Carlson, who says,

225
00:17:17,440 --> 00:17:23,500
The Bible isn't just about what happens, but it's about what always happens.

226
00:17:23,500 --> 00:17:31,100
And so, yes, this is a letter from 4,500 years ago, from a prophet to Jews set in Babylon.

227
00:17:31,860 --> 00:17:40,000
But it's also about how probably people living in a secular culture can navigate these relationships.

228
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:45,700
See, throughout Scripture, Babylon, yes, Babylon is in real place.

229
00:17:45,700 --> 00:17:46,560
This happened.

230
00:17:46,560 --> 00:17:47,340
This is historical.

231
00:17:47,340 --> 00:17:50,060
We could back it up about theology and history.

232
00:17:50,060 --> 00:17:50,560
This happened.

233
00:17:50,760 --> 00:18:04,660
But, throughout Scripture, Babylon isn't just a physical place, but it's symbolic for, it's a picture of any kingdom that sets itself up against the kingdom of God, that counterfeits the things of God.

234
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:26,780
So, yes, Babylon is a real place, but it also is this biblical concept of secular cultures that sets themselves up against the things of God.

235
00:18:27,120 --> 00:18:36,940
Not only is Babylon a symbol for secular cultures, but exiles in Scripture has become a way that most often God's people exist.

236
00:18:36,940 --> 00:18:41,480
Like, just retrace the history of the nation of Israel.

237
00:18:42,200 --> 00:18:44,720
Like, oftentimes they find themselves as an exile.

238
00:18:44,720 --> 00:18:46,520
Look at the history of the church.

239
00:18:46,520 --> 00:18:58,000
Oftentimes, followers of God find themselves powerless and overseen by secular governments and cultures.

240
00:18:58,860 --> 00:19:06,500
And so, yes, Jeremiah is writing two specific exiles in Babylon, but I think we can draw out some principles and options.

241
00:19:06,500 --> 00:19:11,720
We find ourselves in 2023 in America, a close, increasingly post-Christian culture.

242
00:19:11,720 --> 00:19:14,820
How do we navigate these questions?

243
00:19:14,820 --> 00:19:19,760
And can I say, again, I think I said this a little bit earlier.

244
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:28,440
You hear the word exile, and you're like, I don't want a reference, right?

245
00:19:28,440 --> 00:19:30,140
Right?

246
00:19:30,140 --> 00:19:37,500
And I think this is why the church previously, and the generation before, worked really hard to, like, gain political power,

247
00:19:37,500 --> 00:19:39,360
because nobody wants to be powerless.

248
00:19:39,360 --> 00:19:41,260
We want influence.

249
00:19:41,260 --> 00:19:42,080
We want power.

250
00:19:42,080 --> 00:19:51,140
But look at the history of the church, and it grows most when it seemingly has no influence with power.

251
00:19:52,000 --> 00:20:02,060
A group of exiles written according to the principles of God and in the cultures that sets itself up against the things of God

252
00:20:02,060 --> 00:20:05,460
is one of the things that God uses most to build this church.

253
00:20:05,460 --> 00:20:18,700
So, this is what Jeremiah writes to exiles in Babylon, but I think we can essentially say this is what God would say to us

254
00:20:18,700 --> 00:20:25,920
to find ourselves as exiles in a post-Christian culture in America in 2023.

255
00:20:25,920 --> 00:20:29,640
Jeremiah says, 21, 21, this one.

256
00:20:29,640 --> 00:20:34,860
These are the words of the letter that Jeremiah and the prophets sent from Jerusalem to the surviving elders of the exiles

257
00:20:34,860 --> 00:20:42,500
and to the priests, the prophets, and all the people who Meditizer had taken into exile from Jerusalem to Babylon.

258
00:20:42,500 --> 00:20:44,340
Verse 4.

259
00:20:44,340 --> 00:20:45,060
Jeremiah says,

260
00:20:45,060 --> 00:20:46,660
Thus says the Lord.

261
00:20:46,660 --> 00:20:53,560
This is what the Lord says to you as you are an exile in a nation that literally hates all of the things that you believe to be true.

262
00:20:53,560 --> 00:21:01,800
Then says the Lord of hosts, the God of Israel, to all the exiles whom I have sent into exile from Jerusalem.

263
00:21:01,800 --> 00:21:03,260
So, notice this wasn't necessary.

264
00:21:03,260 --> 00:21:04,760
God allowed this to happen.

265
00:21:04,760 --> 00:21:08,780
Build houses and live in them.

266
00:21:08,780 --> 00:21:11,020
Plant gardens and eat their produce.

267
00:21:11,020 --> 00:21:14,000
Take wives and have your sons and daughters.

268
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:20,200
Take wives to your sons and give your daughters a marriage that they need their sons and daughters and multiply there.

269
00:21:20,200 --> 00:21:21,580
And do not eat trees.

270
00:21:22,840 --> 00:21:27,880
So, up to this point, the exiles would have been like, yeah, that's what we do.

271
00:21:27,880 --> 00:21:29,620
Like, that's what Israel has always done.

272
00:21:29,620 --> 00:21:33,480
Israel has always, like, formed this community of other Jewish people.

273
00:21:33,480 --> 00:21:35,460
They've kept to their identity.

274
00:21:35,460 --> 00:21:37,940
And then they just trust God with the rest.

275
00:21:37,940 --> 00:21:39,240
And empires fall.

276
00:21:39,240 --> 00:21:43,060
And whatever happens, they're a tight-knit group.

277
00:21:43,060 --> 00:21:45,280
And so, they would have been tracking with this.

278
00:21:45,900 --> 00:21:56,960
But then, verse 7, but, fight back against the culture of Babylon and the people of Babylon.

279
00:21:56,960 --> 00:21:58,700
Say that.

280
00:21:58,700 --> 00:22:07,740
Say, seek the welfare of the city where I have sent you into exile and pray to the Lord on its behalf for its welfare.

281
00:22:07,960 --> 00:22:10,280
For in its welfare, you will find welfare.

282
00:22:10,280 --> 00:22:17,980
Thus says the Lord of hosts, the God of Israel, do not let your prophets and your visitors who are among you deceive you.

283
00:22:17,980 --> 00:22:20,240
And do not listen to the dreams that they dream.

284
00:22:20,240 --> 00:22:23,580
For it is a lie that are prophesying to you in my name.

285
00:22:23,580 --> 00:22:27,440
I did not send them to close the Lord.

286
00:22:27,440 --> 00:22:34,760
So, in a situation where it seems like Israel might only have three options,

287
00:22:36,360 --> 00:22:39,420
it seems like Jeremiah is giving them a foresight.

288
00:22:39,420 --> 00:22:41,540
Right?

289
00:22:41,540 --> 00:22:46,540
It feels like maybe fighting back against this culture of godless people might be our option.

290
00:22:46,540 --> 00:22:49,740
We get together with strong, powerful, influential people,

291
00:22:49,740 --> 00:22:54,100
and then we can form groups that have power and influence, and we can fight back.

292
00:22:54,100 --> 00:22:58,740
Or maybe we just withdraw and create these holy huddles,

293
00:22:58,740 --> 00:23:02,820
where we don't interact with people at all outside of these walls,

294
00:23:02,820 --> 00:23:05,040
or maybe we just conform, we just become Babylonian,

295
00:23:05,160 --> 00:23:08,600
and we'll be safe, and everything will be good, and we'll be comfortable, and life will be great.

296
00:23:08,600 --> 00:23:12,660
Jeremiah seems to say,

297
00:23:12,660 --> 00:23:14,400
those aren't a good option.

298
00:23:14,400 --> 00:23:16,640
Those are better option.

299
00:23:16,640 --> 00:23:19,420
He seems to say,

300
00:23:19,420 --> 00:23:22,740
don't fight back against the culture.

301
00:23:23,880 --> 00:23:28,540
Because when we fight back against the culture, we lose sight of who the real enemy is.

302
00:23:28,540 --> 00:23:33,540
I've seen this play out so often in the church in America.

303
00:23:33,540 --> 00:23:37,380
When the church fights back against the culture,

304
00:23:37,380 --> 00:23:39,900
it makes the people of the culture respond.

305
00:23:39,900 --> 00:23:46,540
We make the very people that Jesus Christ died for the enemy of the church.

306
00:23:46,620 --> 00:23:50,220
We fight back not against the ideas, but against the people.

307
00:23:50,220 --> 00:23:54,580
And Jeremiah is saying, don't fight back against the people.

308
00:23:54,580 --> 00:23:57,300
Remember who the true enemy is.

309
00:23:57,300 --> 00:23:59,060
Ephesians chapter 6 offers this.

310
00:23:59,060 --> 00:24:03,840
We don't wrestle against flesh and blood, but against spiritual forces.

311
00:24:03,840 --> 00:24:09,860
The great enemy of God is the one who is counterfeiting the kingdom of God's real secular culture.

312
00:24:10,040 --> 00:24:12,240
Our enemy is not the people of the culture.

313
00:24:12,240 --> 00:24:15,260
And so fighting is not an option.

314
00:24:15,260 --> 00:24:18,540
Creating culture wars is not an option.

315
00:24:18,540 --> 00:24:24,300
When we get confrontational with the people of Babylon,

316
00:24:24,300 --> 00:24:27,600
we make the very people Jesus died for our enemies.

317
00:24:27,600 --> 00:24:29,380
I love how Rich Valotus says it.

318
00:24:29,380 --> 00:24:33,100
He says, it's a really curious evangelism strategy

319
00:24:33,100 --> 00:24:36,660
to despise the people you're trying to bring to Jesus.

320
00:24:40,040 --> 00:24:45,340
It's a really curious evangelism strategy to despise the people you're trying to bring to Jesus.

321
00:24:45,340 --> 00:24:46,720
And here's the thing.

322
00:24:46,720 --> 00:24:51,240
I don't believe, I know brothers and sisters in Christ

323
00:24:51,240 --> 00:24:54,640
who's kind of taken and fighting back against the culture of its perspective.

324
00:24:54,640 --> 00:24:58,420
And I don't believe that this is what their intention is.

325
00:24:58,420 --> 00:25:03,620
I think slowly over time, that's how our culture interprets it.

326
00:25:03,620 --> 00:25:05,740
They say, these people hate us.

327
00:25:05,740 --> 00:25:08,720
They want nothing to do with us.

328
00:25:08,720 --> 00:25:10,000
They don't listen to us.

329
00:25:10,000 --> 00:25:11,500
They don't talk with us.

330
00:25:11,500 --> 00:25:15,660
They just rally against the things that we value.

331
00:25:15,660 --> 00:25:22,600
And so, when we fight back against the culture,

332
00:25:22,600 --> 00:25:26,160
we make the wrong enemy the enemy.

333
00:25:26,160 --> 00:25:30,580
So, Jeremiah said, don't fight back against the culture.

334
00:25:30,580 --> 00:25:34,080
But he's also saying, don't withdraw from the culture.

335
00:25:34,080 --> 00:25:38,820
They don't just do the Jewish thing and do really good Jews in Babylon

336
00:25:38,820 --> 00:25:41,020
and ignore everything that's going on there.

337
00:25:41,020 --> 00:25:43,640
He says, work for the prosperity of the culture.

338
00:25:43,640 --> 00:25:45,920
Pray for the people of the culture.

339
00:25:45,920 --> 00:25:53,000
And again, I think out of fear and irreverence for holiness,

340
00:25:53,000 --> 00:25:55,440
sometimes we withdraw so much from the culture

341
00:25:55,440 --> 00:25:58,500
because we don't want to conform to the totems of this world.

342
00:25:59,140 --> 00:26:02,040
And so, we create these holy huddles of people that think like us,

343
00:26:02,040 --> 00:26:03,940
talk like us, believe like us, act like us.

344
00:26:03,940 --> 00:26:08,420
And when we withdraw from secular culture,

345
00:26:08,420 --> 00:26:11,920
we give up valuable kingdom influence.

346
00:26:13,420 --> 00:26:17,580
We're making opportunities to demonstrate the thought and life

347
00:26:17,580 --> 00:26:19,860
of Jesus and the culture around them.

348
00:26:19,860 --> 00:26:23,580
Jesus demonstrated for us how to treat idolatrous people

349
00:26:23,580 --> 00:26:25,680
in a secular culture opposed to God's values.

350
00:26:25,680 --> 00:26:30,160
He came to a people that despised him.

351
00:26:30,160 --> 00:26:34,260
The God that created the universe came to earth.

352
00:26:34,260 --> 00:26:39,300
And the people around set him up as their enemy

353
00:26:39,300 --> 00:26:41,920
and he lovingly engaged in a relationship.

354
00:26:41,920 --> 00:26:47,020
So much so that he literally laid down his life for them

355
00:26:47,020 --> 00:26:49,840
to the point that when they were killing him

356
00:26:49,840 --> 00:26:52,320
and mocking him, he looked to the Father

357
00:26:52,320 --> 00:26:55,780
and he said, forgive them.

358
00:26:55,780 --> 00:26:59,320
They're not my enemy.

359
00:26:59,320 --> 00:27:01,800
They don't know what they're doing.

360
00:27:01,800 --> 00:27:06,000
There's been tricked by a concrete culture.

361
00:27:06,140 --> 00:27:09,860
The enemy of God has convinced them that I am their enemy

362
00:27:09,860 --> 00:27:11,460
when really I am their savior.

363
00:27:11,460 --> 00:27:14,060
So, don't put it against them.

364
00:27:14,060 --> 00:27:15,760
Forgive them.

365
00:27:15,760 --> 00:27:18,000
So, they don't know what they're doing.

366
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:24,160
And I think many of us, including myself,

367
00:27:24,160 --> 00:27:27,680
become hard-hearted for the people of culture

368
00:27:27,680 --> 00:27:30,260
or even as our enemies.

369
00:27:30,260 --> 00:27:35,660
Others of us have become so afraid of cultural influences over us

370
00:27:35,660 --> 00:27:38,680
that we've withdrawn, which, yet again,

371
00:27:38,680 --> 00:27:40,460
in just another way, makes them our enemies.

372
00:27:40,460 --> 00:27:44,740
But what if we fought back against both of these perspectives

373
00:27:44,740 --> 00:27:48,180
by intentionally praying for the welfare of the people around us?

374
00:27:48,180 --> 00:27:51,060
Imagine how God might send our hearts

375
00:27:51,060 --> 00:27:52,960
towards people and culture

376
00:27:52,960 --> 00:27:54,480
if we just praise them.

377
00:27:54,480 --> 00:27:57,720
We just engage them in a relationship

378
00:27:57,720 --> 00:28:00,160
when out of our way to intentionally connect.

379
00:28:02,880 --> 00:28:06,060
So, not only is fighting or fleeing

380
00:28:06,060 --> 00:28:07,900
not an appropriate response,

381
00:28:07,900 --> 00:28:09,800
but neither is informing.

382
00:28:09,800 --> 00:28:13,720
And this is, for me,

383
00:28:13,720 --> 00:28:16,160
I'm just going to be as vulnerable

384
00:28:16,160 --> 00:28:17,160
and friendly friend as possible.

385
00:28:17,160 --> 00:28:19,700
This is the one that's most tempting for me

386
00:28:19,700 --> 00:28:22,720
because I love people, right?

387
00:28:22,720 --> 00:28:25,380
I want to have a good friendship

388
00:28:25,380 --> 00:28:27,020
with every single one of you in this room,

389
00:28:27,620 --> 00:28:28,640
which is not possible.

390
00:28:28,640 --> 00:28:29,660
But I want it.

391
00:28:29,660 --> 00:28:31,040
Like, I desperately want it.

392
00:28:31,040 --> 00:28:32,240
And so,

393
00:28:32,240 --> 00:28:34,160
I think many Christians,

394
00:28:34,160 --> 00:28:36,080
we read passages like this from Jeremiah,

395
00:28:36,080 --> 00:28:39,360
and we desperately want to love the people of our culture.

396
00:28:39,360 --> 00:28:42,120
We don't want to be competitive or withdrawn,

397
00:28:42,580 --> 00:28:43,800
but what we do instead

398
00:28:43,800 --> 00:28:45,760
is slowly over time

399
00:28:45,760 --> 00:28:48,360
and we just conform to the cultural values.

400
00:28:48,360 --> 00:28:49,740
That's our counterfeit

401
00:28:49,740 --> 00:28:51,540
to the values of the kingdom of God.

402
00:28:51,540 --> 00:28:55,040
And then it's slowly over time

403
00:28:55,040 --> 00:28:56,680
and we make one compromise

404
00:28:56,680 --> 00:28:58,140
and another and another,

405
00:28:58,140 --> 00:28:59,080
and before we know it,

406
00:28:59,080 --> 00:29:01,140
there's nothing distinct about us

407
00:29:01,140 --> 00:29:02,040
as Christ followers

408
00:29:02,040 --> 00:29:04,820
from anyone else who doesn't follow Jesus.

409
00:29:04,820 --> 00:29:09,200
And what God is not calling the Jewish upsellers to do

410
00:29:09,200 --> 00:29:11,000
is to conform to Babylonian culture.

411
00:29:11,000 --> 00:29:13,720
He wants them to flourish in Babylon

412
00:29:13,720 --> 00:29:15,520
distinctly as Jews

413
00:29:15,520 --> 00:29:18,020
while they work for the placing

414
00:29:18,020 --> 00:29:19,360
of the Babylonian culture.

415
00:29:19,360 --> 00:29:22,380
So,

416
00:29:22,380 --> 00:29:24,880
it's not our job

417
00:29:24,880 --> 00:29:27,780
to hold non-Christians

418
00:29:27,780 --> 00:29:30,200
accountable to the standards

419
00:29:30,200 --> 00:29:31,020
of the kingdom of God.

420
00:29:31,020 --> 00:29:34,140
They don't agree with those ideas.

421
00:29:34,140 --> 00:29:36,620
But it's also not our job

422
00:29:36,620 --> 00:29:40,440
to pretend like they're not valuable to us,

423
00:29:40,440 --> 00:29:43,100
like they're not important to us.

424
00:29:43,100 --> 00:29:44,100
We don't apologize

425
00:29:44,100 --> 00:29:45,120
or shrink up

426
00:29:45,120 --> 00:29:46,820
from living distantly

427
00:29:46,820 --> 00:29:48,220
in light of the kingdom of God.

428
00:29:48,220 --> 00:29:50,300
We distinctly follow Jesus

429
00:29:50,300 --> 00:29:51,320
in any culture

430
00:29:51,320 --> 00:29:53,200
that is opposed to the things of Jesus.

431
00:29:53,200 --> 00:29:55,360
And we do so lovingly

432
00:29:55,360 --> 00:29:57,500
with compassion and intentionality

433
00:29:57,500 --> 00:29:58,080
in prayer.

434
00:29:58,080 --> 00:30:00,120
Jesus says this

435
00:30:00,120 --> 00:30:01,100
in Matthew chapter 5.

436
00:30:01,100 --> 00:30:04,400
For the temptation to conform.

437
00:30:05,280 --> 00:30:05,600
He says,

438
00:30:05,600 --> 00:30:07,600
You are the salt of the earth.

439
00:30:07,600 --> 00:30:11,660
But salt loses its saltiness.

440
00:30:11,660 --> 00:30:14,380
How can it be made salt to you again?

441
00:30:14,380 --> 00:30:17,220
It is no longer good for anything.

442
00:30:17,220 --> 00:30:17,620
He says,

443
00:30:17,620 --> 00:30:20,000
If you lose your distinctness,

444
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:23,400
if you stop being distinctly a follower of Jesus,

445
00:30:23,400 --> 00:30:25,500
then you won't be an influence

446
00:30:25,500 --> 00:30:26,760
on the culture around you.

447
00:30:26,760 --> 00:30:27,740
You will be useless

448
00:30:27,740 --> 00:30:29,860
to the culture around you.

449
00:30:30,440 --> 00:30:32,220
You are the light of the world,

450
00:30:32,220 --> 00:30:33,580
a town built on a hill

451
00:30:33,580 --> 00:30:34,860
that cannot be hidden either.

452
00:30:34,860 --> 00:30:36,560
And people light a lamp

453
00:30:36,560 --> 00:30:37,740
and put it under a bulb.

454
00:30:37,740 --> 00:30:38,940
Instead,

455
00:30:38,940 --> 00:30:40,400
they put it on a stand

456
00:30:40,400 --> 00:30:41,300
and they give light

457
00:30:41,300 --> 00:30:42,600
to everyone in the house.

458
00:30:42,600 --> 00:30:43,460
In the same way,

459
00:30:43,460 --> 00:30:45,440
let your light shine before others

460
00:30:45,440 --> 00:30:46,480
that they may see

461
00:30:46,480 --> 00:30:47,500
your good deeds

462
00:30:47,500 --> 00:30:49,220
and glorify your Father in all.

463
00:30:51,220 --> 00:30:52,580
This is Jesus saying

464
00:30:52,580 --> 00:30:53,700
what Jeremiah was saying

